%I A399515 #17 Oct 11 2026 16:59:06
%S A399515 13,21,31,32,43,44,45,57,58,59,73,74,75,76,91,92,93,94,95,111,112,113,
%T A399515 114,115,116,133,134,135,136,137,138,139,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,
%U A399515 183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,211,212,213,214,215,216,217,218,219,241,242,243,244,245,246
%N A399515 Numbers a for which there are smaller integers b > c > d > 0 such that c^2 = a + d and d^2 = b + c.
%C A399515 The equations may be written as c = sqrt(a + d) and d = sqrt(b + c). Then, recursively substituting d and c in the right hand side (RHS) by the expression given in the other RHS, leads to an infinitely nested radical c = sqrt(a + sqrt(b + sqrt(a + ...))), and similarly for d, with b and a exchanged.
%C A399515 We can choose d >= 3 and then c > d, c < d^2/2, which gives round(d^2/2) - d - 1 = floor((d^2-1)/2 - d) solutions, with b = d^2 - c > c and a = c^2 - d > b + c + d.
%C A399515 The sequence does not contain any square. The jumps or gaps g(n) = a(n+1) - a(n) > 1 occur exactly around the squares >= 4^2 = 16, i.e., where a(n) < k^2 < a(n+1), k >= 4. The indices n = n(k-3) where this occurs are listed in A399516. The gaps g(n) > 1 are strictly increasing and yield all integers >= 8 except those which are in A080827.
%C A399515 An integer a(n) is in the sequence if and only if c = floor(sqrt(a(n)))+1 satisfies d := c^2 - a(n) < c < d^2/2.
%F A399515 a(n+1) = a(n) + 1 except for n = 1, 2, 4, 7, 10, ... = A399516, which differs from A196126 after 77.
%F A399515 For j = A399516(n), a(j) < (n+3)^2 < a(j+1), and g(n) = a(j+1) - a(j) = 8, 10, 11, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17, 18, 20, 21, ... = { k >= 8 | k not in A080827 }: The numbers > 8 not occurring as gaps are 9, 13, 19, 25, 33, ... = A080827[4..] = A099392[5..] (different from A085913 for values >= 1799).
%e A399515 a(1) = 13 because for b = 5, c = 4 and d = 3 we have c^2 = a + d and d^2 = b + c.
%e A399515 a(2) = 21 because for b = 11, c = 5 and d = 4 we have c^2 = a + d and d^2 = b + c.
%o A399515 (PARI) select( {is_A399515(n) = my(c=sqrtint(n)+1, d=c^2-n); d < c && c < d^2\/2}, [1..246])
%Y A399515 Cf. A080827 and A099392 (give numbers > 8 that don't occur as first differences).
%Y A399515 Cf. A399516 (indices where jumps occur).
%K A399515 nonn,new
%O A399515 1,1
%A A399515 _M. F. Hasler_, Oct 02 2026
